  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GCA-IP2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The two associations have decided to collaborate on developing common objectives, in particular those that support a world based onrelationships of solidarity and greater justice. The two associations agree that respect for Human Rights, including the Rights of Women and Children, forms part of their commitment, as well as respect for Social and Economic Rights for everyone. The Action that is subject to the present agreement is a contribution towards these objectives, but it cannot be considered as thesole link that unites the three associations.

The partner-LDPA and Oxfam-in-Laos undertake to build a relationship that reinforces each party&#x2019;s work and skills, while developing each organisation&#x2019;s respective strategies.

By way of an example, LDPA is interested in taking part in activities that heighten awareness among the Laos public, by sending personnel and/or equipment in relation to the issue concerned by the Action. LDPA would also like to take part in the discussions held by the Oxfam in Laoson Strategic Reflections connected with the action</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Community Alliance (GCA )</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green community alliance (GCA) is a local non-profit association. The main vision of the association is to deliver land/natural resources-based policy and legal awareness for rural communities of Laos. GCA has a role in strengthening rural ethnic communities# knowledge with regards to conservation and sustainable use of natural resources including land; promoting sustainable livelihoods and reforestation.
GCA is a relatively small and young organization if compared with others Civil Society Organizations at both national and regional level.  The organization currently has 8 staff members and over 10 of volunteers who have graduated from bachelor and master degrees in relevant subject areas including: forestry, environmental management, human and social sciences.
In line with our organization capacity building policies, GCA supports their team leader and other staff members to participate in the various training courses at national and international such as: CCA and Improving Forest Governance in CIDT-England</narrative>
  </participating-org>
